  "solution_principle": "VERY IMPORTANT!\r\n\r\nBe careful which components you choose!\r\nSometimes, components may give the same results visually, but they may have different impacts on the long run, and that could creat problems.\r\n\r\nAlways double check the result comprehensively in order to avoid problems.\r\n\r\nExample below:\r\n\r\nBoundary Surface results into a \"Trimmed Surface\".\r\n\r\nLoft results into an \"Untrimmed Surface\".\r\n\r\nBoth results work fine. But if you want to make surface divisions, differences are very big and could make you choose which component to beging with!\r\n\r\nIn this case, Loft works better because in results into an \"Untrimmed Surface\", which would be a good start for surface division!",
